abstract: >-
  UOHF Definition 2.1 defines human function as the body's capacity to be
  appropriately engaged to meet internal and external demands. It provides a
  governed ontology and semantic-rule architecture for demand, functional
  engagement, state inference, safety constraints, action, feedback,
  longitudinal individual modeling, and the Human Function World Model.
